![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Use optional chaining when finding specific fixtures to prevent a `TypeError` if any fixture in the array is nullish or malformed.

```suggestion
  const acceptedFixture = fixtures.fixture_results.find((fixture) => fixture?.fixture_id === 'accepted_fact');
  const provisionalFixture = fixtures.fixture_results.find((fixture) => (
    fixture?.fixture_id === 'provisional_downgraded_context'
  ));
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When filtering or mapping arrays of objects, use defensive guards (such as checking if the element is a valid object) to ignore nullish or malformed elements instead of throwing a TypeError.
</details>

