Use optional chaining and defensive checks when filtering and verifying fallback behavior to prevent a `TypeError` if any fixture or its pack is nullish or malformed.

```suggestion
  const fallbackFixtures = fixtures.fixture_results.filter((fixture) => (
    fixture?.pack?.fallback_behavior?.enabled === true
  ));
  const fallbackAttemptsAvailable = fallbackFixtures.every((fixture) => (
    fixture?.pack?.question_attempt_available === true
  ));
  const fallbackNoInvention = fallbackFixtures.every((fixture) => (
    fixture?.pack?.fallback_behavior?.no_invention_constraints &&
    JSON.stringify(fixture.pack.fallback_behavior.no_invention_constraints) ===
    JSON.stringify(NO_INVENTION_CONSTRAINTS)
  ));
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When filtering or mapping arrays of objects, use defensive guards (such as checking if the element is a valid object) to ignore nullish or malformed elements instead of throwing a TypeError.
</details>

